<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Niagara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Niagara is a fortress at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niagara-river">Niagara River</a> on Lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> State. The French built a stone 'French Castle' there in 1726 to control the route to the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a>. British forces captured it after a siege in July 1759, and it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1796. Restored, it is now a historic site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-niagara.jpg" alt="Fort Niagara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ad Meskens · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:French_castle_at_Fort_Niagara_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
